[{:db/id "q-89347/selection/cf4007c3fa4151e57698e948ec1fea6bf9b3de5d146d298803d0412645d0248d" :answer/id #uuid "643a4bb6-ecd5-5d11-bb9b-2e1773973ddd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89347/selection/b99a41c2495bc5629f5e19e5dd0eb7719a9a673afa058fcedfb87312b0b99f96" :answer/id #uuid "6240f72a-0d02-5d66-bf9c-695aad894866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89347/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" :answer/id #uuid "38bc38bc-4117-5713-bcc7-f41bb36fdc4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89347/selection/b85ba2ba54d596653a563476b4f78775ae06d7693e7e2bfe7b1bde461b8c1155" :answer/id #uuid "8a68e4a6-0103-5b47-bebc-81ac24dd3af5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89347/selection/1be01a38655c9b80c5143f8e1af887b96d6afac0d8b99aa5a70070b461be0f30" :answer/id #uuid "fcdc42b4-c773-5263-b22c-7ab06b99321c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89347/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "61d234ec-66e7-50ac-b720-163a2cf9d3df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89347/selection/1be01a38655c9b80c5143f8e1af887b96d6afac0d8b99aa5a70070b461be0f30" :answer-field/choices ["q-89347/selection/cf4007c3fa4151e57698e948ec1fea6bf9b3de5d146d298803d0412645d0248d" "q-89347/selection/b99a41c2495bc5629f5e19e5dd0eb7719a9a673afa058fcedfb87312b0b99f96" "q-89347/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" "q-89347/selection/b85ba2ba54d596653a563476b4f78775ae06d7693e7e2bfe7b1bde461b8c1155" "q-89347/selection/1be01a38655c9b80c5143f8e1af887b96d6afac0d8b99aa5a70070b461be0f30"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89347" :question/id #uuid "698299c1-e40e-528b-a38d-66f6a77ea0e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-89347" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/a2f0f570ecc68de1a5b34fb3bd1b341fc83a728b026b035dde848dbf986e441b.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/e7ef7fd90c828767359daf69f68f406d61e3f82ad86b1f6b3a9480c99dedadf8.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0],$ we get the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-89347/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14527450-9b34-5982-9d87-b5a31870a70e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89347"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106515/selection/5461977dfaa2efa547dbedd51224463dffb514fb803bd894735918a5170bb0ef" :answer/id #uuid "a9540f92-2168-5a93-a628-95b476ae8485" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106515/selection/3f265a027ccf1edb6dc4c84e73d156c98aa4f8fc3d80f32297ef6c675f4577ef" :answer/id #uuid "54c2b402-6c68-5158-8eb1-5542167e0147" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106515/selection/f20c98fc3c3b3327e4fd73cdf4c095fddfd0abcd259a974390ebd99675903afe" :answer/id #uuid "9ab57bf2-3206-5bf8-90bb-acd50bf3920f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106515/selection/a3e029fe068645305b6c3cee302f1755dec73bd764dbd5b19ae144dda87b5417" :answer/id #uuid "433a0cc0-92ab-5848-a30d-8196027c8e58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106515/selection/c98c43749d1741371dba606ca47b69b3e42ad8ae36d1f6b902c73d9c65bc06b7" :answer/id #uuid "8695d525-6e49-5e1c-8dc5-d4e1ed229ad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106515/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3bed314-7cf9-50a5-92f1-b263d5bf76f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106515/selection/f20c98fc3c3b3327e4fd73cdf4c095fddfd0abcd259a974390ebd99675903afe" :answer-field/choices ["q-106515/selection/5461977dfaa2efa547dbedd51224463dffb514fb803bd894735918a5170bb0ef" "q-106515/selection/3f265a027ccf1edb6dc4c84e73d156c98aa4f8fc3d80f32297ef6c675f4577ef" "q-106515/selection/f20c98fc3c3b3327e4fd73cdf4c095fddfd0abcd259a974390ebd99675903afe" "q-106515/selection/a3e029fe068645305b6c3cee302f1755dec73bd764dbd5b19ae144dda87b5417" "q-106515/selection/c98c43749d1741371dba606ca47b69b3e42ad8ae36d1f6b902c73d9c65bc06b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106515" :question/id #uuid "57a70c61-ca1c-517f-b49f-a1db49c2f10a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106515" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/999d1d14a31f9619306efe6b1c2ebc6e900a52bf4e2d2edd7230e7dd7c9b25b9.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm 2x.$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(1,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=1.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm 2x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\ \\frac{b}{1} & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106515/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32fc8440-e872-50e4-ab98-5861d1c7310e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106515"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106517/selection/d01d12b2d18fa820b896ca493e25dcfc99ca6af0e889f04d3e3361c4c96ba2cf" :answer/id #uuid "0b09fed6-9bf8-522c-a457-2f7e4f4f1d06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106517/selection/f6aa3b88647279edc479300b439dd184b93c91468e7b7168b015c124715b6e85" :answer/id #uuid "ba06d81e-e540-5865-a9f8-3d5727309dc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106517/selection/cfde77495b650d97a781f165ce5753448e80da8fca7933a37398dc15459451f2" :answer/id #uuid "48bb799a-2e2a-5921-b3c8-961cc33efbe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106517/selection/bba0a450741f4ef42007000978d33fd2caf429d09f6e904d9fc3ed943893c1d1" :answer/id #uuid "7679a998-15be-54ad-a2e3-ca88f39fdd7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106517/selection/5b80ce30bc1316f64fd4ba3931d37c1143306138f49888f37c1f35f5a41307db" :answer/id #uuid "4472205c-c0c7-5cf9-8946-6e05f17bf732" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106517/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90b838b8-e502-5a6e-b66a-3e1a9a75cd86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106517/selection/5b80ce30bc1316f64fd4ba3931d37c1143306138f49888f37c1f35f5a41307db" :answer-field/choices ["q-106517/selection/d01d12b2d18fa820b896ca493e25dcfc99ca6af0e889f04d3e3361c4c96ba2cf" "q-106517/selection/f6aa3b88647279edc479300b439dd184b93c91468e7b7168b015c124715b6e85" "q-106517/selection/cfde77495b650d97a781f165ce5753448e80da8fca7933a37398dc15459451f2" "q-106517/selection/bba0a450741f4ef42007000978d33fd2caf429d09f6e904d9fc3ed943893c1d1" "q-106517/selection/5b80ce30bc1316f64fd4ba3931d37c1143306138f49888f37c1f35f5a41307db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106517" :question/id #uuid "731d98b7-b827-5e98-bc4b-a4e46aa03b9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106517" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/b570ce72a87d7583a230ea1c863656f982c7fefeb546295d41429876cc823837.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(2,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=2.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{b}{2} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ b & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106517/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32fc8440-e872-50e4-ab98-5861d1c7310e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106517"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106524/selection/097c3cca32afadfc847d39108d23f10d9c55c57c1b14a26b233b428c3d901ef7" :answer/id #uuid "b8043a04-4ad9-5068-ab03-9534e2632810" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106524/selection/e46a04253e451ec3ccf92bf9b6feec2f8e9de1a7a0ddf564af9c8e44d19d2fd5" :answer/id #uuid "06837e4a-132e-5d28-8d49-2cb8e24af5e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106524/selection/bdda3298b2c245f24dc56b02b943006bd312eda6367fca6149614b593e6c715d" :answer/id #uuid "f577bed4-fd4a-50cc-81ae-9571a81b010f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106524/selection/f6e269e6946b6a4d8f07d4265687baf9be4c93e667ce24a1d6e8ed2cbce8d8c4" :answer/id #uuid "94369efc-c634-5d2d-80a4-2f8a3d5ebe95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106524/selection/5a5311d6a036dac7501951ddba3d2bb7cfbad2783f210b143a38d689ec4a4190" :answer/id #uuid "5b8a8c4a-0cf9-556e-88c1-cb015567883e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106524/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3f250da-1e15-5918-96f9-0b43d8fd1ada" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106524/selection/bdda3298b2c245f24dc56b02b943006bd312eda6367fca6149614b593e6c715d" :answer-field/choices ["q-106524/selection/097c3cca32afadfc847d39108d23f10d9c55c57c1b14a26b233b428c3d901ef7" "q-106524/selection/e46a04253e451ec3ccf92bf9b6feec2f8e9de1a7a0ddf564af9c8e44d19d2fd5" "q-106524/selection/bdda3298b2c245f24dc56b02b943006bd312eda6367fca6149614b593e6c715d" "q-106524/selection/f6e269e6946b6a4d8f07d4265687baf9be4c93e667ce24a1d6e8ed2cbce8d8c4" "q-106524/selection/5a5311d6a036dac7501951ddba3d2bb7cfbad2783f210b143a38d689ec4a4190"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106524" :question/id #uuid "7c274a2a-ce8f-57fe-a73e-45cba23684ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-106524" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106524/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6ebe1f1-40fe-5226-8aed-b321f2e1e58b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106524"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325941/field-1/ea2e49fef6877eda8df0a35cff1716c7703fc8e6ec46106bfbfaffa37eb45131" :answer/id #uuid "6aecc25a-0f60-5138-81de-6ca15b6da3fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{100}-\\frac{y^2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325941/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc2677a1-f592-567d-a53c-95d35518b2b5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325941/field-1/ea2e49fef6877eda8df0a35cff1716c7703fc8e6ec46106bfbfaffa37eb45131" :answer-field/choices ["q-325941/field-1/ea2e49fef6877eda8df0a35cff1716c7703fc8e6ec46106bfbfaffa37eb45131"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325941" :question/id #uuid "4a34c59e-1cd9-5fb4-9616-c68d076c6f17" :question/math-academy-id "q-325941" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=10\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =10\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{10} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{10}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{100} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{100} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{100}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-325941/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6ebe1f1-40fe-5226-8aed-b321f2e1e58b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325941"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
